  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The informal workers continue to face many challenges in exercising their fundamentals labour rights, including, among others, freedom of association and the effective recognition of the right to collective bargaining; the elimination of forced or compulsory labour; the abolition of child labour; and the elimination of discrimination in respect of employment and occupation &#x2013; as well as other rights such as the right to a workplace free of violence, and safe working conditions.

The Confederation of Mongolian Trade Unions (CMTU) discusses the need to ensure workers&#x2019; right to freedom of association and strengthen the trade unions movement in their development programme for 2017-2030. As part of this effort, they aim  to launch campaigns to organize workers in the private sector and the informal economy, with the goal of increasing trade union membership by at least 7% annually.

Hence the work envisaged for the biennium looks at how best CMTU can be supported to enhance their membership services so that the stated goals can be better facilitated. 

The ILO Country Office in Mongolia launched its initiative on the subject by way of undertaking activities under its new project - Fostering the Transition to Formality of Informal Workers and Economic Units in Mongolia as of 1st April 2023 running up to March 2025. 

In addition, ILO supports Workers&#x2019; organizations in offering new services designed for workers in facilitating the transition to formality. This includes support to develop a phone application for its members to deliver services effectively.</narrative>
  </description>
